! The multi-species linear cases are ELECTROMAGNETIC.  A second kinetic species
! and a finite beta are the two ingredients that between them broke the momentum
! budget, and testing them together linearly -- where every channel is either
! zero or exactly one thing -- is far sharper than waiting for the nonlinear
! cases to expose them.  This is also the only place in the set where gbar, the
! parallel Ampere solve and the vpar-dApar part of the advecting velocity are
! exercised without turbulence on top.
! MULTIPLE KINETIC SPECIES, linear.  This case exists because it is the one that
! found a real bug.  With every channel identically zero and nothing driving the
! projection, a second kinetic species still degraded conservation tenfold, and
! neither a sixteenfold smaller time step nor a fourfold finer grid moved it --
! which is what identified the momentum inertia's missing parallel-velocity
! normalisation.  A single-species linear case cannot see that error, because for
! m = T = 1 the wrong coefficient and the right one are the same number.
! Run length.  At nstep = 600 (t = 30) the drift channel -- the only source in
! this case -- had not moved the flow far enough to test anything: the energy
! turnover was 0.086, so the budget was satisfied whether the diagnostic was
! right or not.  It is NOT the field line: alpha0 = 0, 0.35, 0.7, 1.05 and 1.57
! all give turnovers between 0.03 and 0.15.  It is the run length.  At
! nstep = 6000 (t = 300) the turnover is 1.9 and the case becomes a real test of
! the drift channel, which is what it exists for.  nstep = 3000 is enough on
! paper -- it gives 0.88 -- but the turnover is not reproducible to better than a
! factor of two between invocations, and a run of that length came back at 0.49
! on one of them, just under the threshold, which skips the assertion and passes
! vacuously.  Twice the length puts it clear of that boundary.  The phi_RH residual then
! settles at 1.5e-01: 1.81e-01 at t = 30, 1.52e-01 at t = 150, 1.47e-01 at
! t = 300, so it is a converged measurement of the drift-channel defect rather
! than a transient.
!
! Omega_RH stays vacuous even here, turnover 0.09, and rises only to 0.24 by
! t = 300.  That is structural rather than a matter of length: the secular drift
! is carried mostly by trapped particles and W^[Omega] vanishes on trapped
! orbits, so the drift channel has very little purchase on the odd invariant.
! Case 1: linear, collisionless.
! W7-X, zonal mode at kx rho = 0.2.
! Rosenbluth-Hinton energy budget in W7X geometry: linear zonal flow with
! collisional damping.  A single zonal mode initialised with ginit_option='rh'
! and relaxed by Dougherty collisions.  The run is linear, so the nonlinear RH
! fluxes vanish and the budget is driven by the collisional channel together
! with the magnetic-drift channel, which is what distinguishes this from the
! tokamak benchmark: in an axisymmetric field the bounce-averaged radial drift
! vanishes and P_drift with it, while here it is the dominant source.
&parameters_physics
  nonlinear = .false.
  vnew_ref = 0.1
  include_apar = .true.
  include_bpar = .true.
  beta = 4.0e-3
/
&kt_grids_knobs
  grid_option = 'range'
/
&kt_grids_range_parameters
  naky = 1
  aky_min = 0.0
  akx_min = 0.2
  nakx = 1
/
! The linear cases are initialised with BOTH a density perturbation and a
! parallel flow.  Starting from a zonal potential alone leaves the momentum
! projection near zero, and normalising by it inflates the residual into a
! defect that is not there; starting from a flow alone does the same to the
! potential projection.  Exciting both is what makes one run test both.
&init_g_knobs
  ginit_option = 'default'
  phiinit = 1.0
  den0 = 1.0
  upar0 = 1.0
  width0 = 1.0
/
&species_knobs
  nspec = 2
/
&species_parameters_1
  dens = 1.0
  fprim = 0.0
  mass = 1.0
  temp = 1.0
  tprim = 0.0
  type = 'ion'
  z = 1.0
/
&species_parameters_2
  dens = 1.0
  fprim = 2.2
  mass = 2.7e-4
  temp = 1.0
  tprim = 8.0
  type = 'electron'
  z = -1.0
/
&zgrid_parameters
  boundary_option = 'unconnected'
  nperiod = 1
  nzed = 128
/
&vpamu_grids_parameters
  nmu = 24
  nvgrid = 48
/
&knobs
  delt = 0.05
  nstep = 6000
  print_extra_info_to_terminal = .false.
  drifts_implicit = .true.
/
&stella_diagnostics_knobs
  nsave = -1
  nwrite = 1
  save_for_restart = .false.
  write_RH_integrands = .false.
  write_RH_inertia_fluxes = .true.
/
&geo_knobs
  geo_option = 'vmec'
/
&vmec_parameters
  nfield_periods = 8
  torflux = 0.5
  alpha0 = 0.7
  vmec_filename = 'wout_QA.nc'
/
&dissipation
  include_collisions = .false.
  collision_model = 'dougherty'
  hyper_dissipation = .false.
/
